// The Kalphite Queen's animations, both forms, from the Old School cache - needed because both
// forms now wear Old School's meshes (area_kalphite/configs/kalphite.npc says why) and a 377 seq
// moves nothing on an Old School mesh: the vertex labels are a different skeleton's.
//
// Her two forms are rigged separately, and every seq below is on the skeleton its form's mesh
// carries - crawling form on 1422, flying form on 1425. Each form's own block is five seqs, the
// usual walk / ready / attack / block / death. The cache states walk and ready in the npc record
// (6238 and 6239 for the first form, 6236 for the second, all three already converted for the
// Kalphite Princess pet); the other three per form were identified by rendering each candidate onto
// the queen's own mesh with tools/models/posepreview.py and looking at it:
//
//   6240  first form, attack      the head rears back and strikes down
//   6241  first form, block       ten frames, flinches and recovers to the ready pose
//   6242  first form, death       ends collapsed and flat - and this IS the shell cracking open,
//                                 which is why kalphite_queen.rs2 plays it on the corpse npc
//   6234  flying form, attack     pitches forward, wings back
//   6235  flying form, attack     the second of the flying form's two, for its claws/mandibles roll
//   6237  flying form, block      eight frames, the shortest on skeleton 1425
//   6233  flying form, death      sinks to the ground and stays there
//   6270  flying form, rising     sixty-nine frames from nothing to the full standing pose: the
//                                 flying queen unfolding out of the first form's shell
//
// The workers, soldiers, guardians and lords keep their 377 models, so they keep the 377 kalphite
// seqs in kalphite.seq. Nothing here is shared with them.
// Animations converted from the OSRS cache by tools/models/animconvosrs.py.
// They play on the OSRS player skeleton (base_osrs_*), not the 377 one: the client
// only walk-merges two animations that share a base (ClientPlayer/NpcType patch).

[osrs_seq_6240]
// OSRS seq 6240
walkmerge=label_1,label_2,label_3,label_6,label_8,label_10,label_12,label_14,label_16,label_18,label_20,label_22,label_24,label_26,label_28,label_30,label_32,label_34,label_36,label_38,label_40,label_42,label_44,label_46,label_48,label_50,label_52,label_196,label_197,label_198
